AB  - Agentic AI represents a fundamental shift from reactive, model-centric paradigms toward autonomous, goal-directed systems capable of reasoning, adaptation, and coordinated action in dynamic environments. This paper presents a comprehensive systematic survey and a unified multidimensional taxonomy of Agentic AI, structuring the literature across six interrelated dimensions: architectural paradigms, cognitive foundations, interaction and adaptation, explainability, security–privacy–safety alignment, and evaluation. The survey synthesizes recent advances in agent architectures, including monolithic, modular, multi-agent, embodied, and tool-augmented systems, highlighting key design principles that support scalability, flexibility, and interoperability. It further examines the cognitive foundations underlying agentic behavior, encompassing goal formation, self-reflection, memory and context persistence, reasoning and planning, and continual learning. The interaction and adaptation dimension analyzes human–AI collaboration, multi-agent coordination, and environment-aware behavior, emphasizing the operation of agents in open, dynamic, and socially situated settings. Explainability is positioned as a core requirement for agentic systems, covering behavioral traceability, goal attribution, and layered explanation frameworks that enable transparency across agent hierarchies. In parallel, the survey reviews security, privacy, and safety-by-design mechanisms, including adversarial robustness, secure tool execution, trust calibration, and human-in-the-loop oversight. Finally, the paper examines evaluation methodologies for Agentic AI, addressing outcome-oriented performance, structural and graph-based analyses, resilience, autonomy–oversight trade-offs, and human-centric assessment criteria. By providing a unified taxonomy and systematic synthesis, this survey establishes a structured foundation for analyzing various existing approaches, identifying open challenges, and guiding future research toward the development of transparent, robust, and trustworthy Agentic AI systems.
ER  - 

