AB  - The rapid evolution of software development is being fundamentally shaped by the integration of Machine learning (ML) and Deep learning (DL) technologies. This chapter provides a broad discourse on next generation software development, including how ML/DL are transforming traditional engineering paradigms into adaptive systems that are data-driven and intelligent systems. The chapter begins with an overview of the theoretical basis for ML and DL and then discusses the complete lifecycle of the development process, starting with the data collection phase, through the feature engineering phase to model deployment and monitoring, with a focus on best practice and architectural patterns, for example, microservices and API-driven integration. Real world examples of case studies including Netflix’s recommendation engine and Google Translate’s language processing tools, highlight and demonstrate the scalable and practical potential that technologies like these can provide to different industries. The chapter also covers other challenges, namely data quality, explainability of models, ethics of AI models and the demands on computational resources and offers tangible recommendations or mitigation strategy. The chapter concludes with considerations of trends such as reinforcement learning, generative adversarial networks, edge computing future possibilities or explainable AI and offers a vision of responsible, innovative, and scalable software systems. The synthesis of the chapter will assist practitioners, researchers and decision-makers with possibilities of and navigating and leading in the evolving era of AI influenced software development.
