AB  - The convergence of Digital Twin (DT) platforms and generative artificial intelligence (Generative AI) is essential for addressing the usability and interpretability constraints of complex smart grid systems. This chapter introduces a modular smart grid architecture model (SGAM) that integrates large language models (LLMs) for semantic reasoning and natural language interaction. The core framework incorporates a knowledge graph (KG) to represent heterogeneous information, enabling retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) workflows for context-aware and trustworthy decision-making. Key deployment considerations are outlined, balancing the advanced capabilities and scalability of cloud-based LLM services with the data privacy and operational control offered by on-premise LLM options. With this integrated approach, DTs turn into proactive, user-friendly systems that enhance data analytics, resource management, and decision-making capabilities for energy infrastructures.
